.next-verify/
# BUILD OUTPUT UNDER ANOTHER NAME.
#
# A build can be pointed at a different directory with PCD_DIST_DIR, which is
# how a verification build runs while a dev server still holds .next. Those
# directories are ordinary build output and must never be committed: each one
# carries a webpack cache of 300MB or so, well past what GitHub will accept,
# and a push carrying them is refused outright.
.nv-*/
.nv*/

